 I. INTRODUCTION
 This paper presents an approach to developing a machine
 learning model aimed at predicting future property value using
 data sourced from the New York City (NYC) Open Data
 using practical implementations and analytical evaluations.
 The steps are covered beginning with data pre-processing,
 model comparison with various classifiers, cross-validation
 techniques, and model optimization. Each stage was designed
 to ensure the accuracy of the predictive model. The key steps
 involved in the process were data imputation, scaling, model
 selection, cross-validation, and optimization.
